{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Yissa.</b> He swears, like \"You shall not take [תשא] the name of YHWH\" (Exodus 20:7)." "<b>Hovesh.</b> Like hovesh makkah (one who dresses a wound), and the meaning is like \"the blind and the lame\" [i.e., one unfit] — וכת׳ יורש עצר (Judges 18:17)." "<b>And there is no garment.</b> Even for myself."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {1 "The citation וכת׳ (וכוותיקין, 'and according to the version') introduces a variant reading of Judges 18:17; the phrase יורש עצר is obscure and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:42.160471210Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}